ng fields. Avoid `@defer` on a\ndeleted record, because deferred fields may need to read the row after it is gone."],[2970,"For an API where direct refetches require a signed-in user, put that requirement on **both**\ngenerated lookup fields. These options belong in the builder's `relay` configuration, alongside\nthe Scope Auth setup shown below. The private-policy example combines these gates with the\nNode interface and Query defaults discussed next; the original example keeps its public\nfeatured-article path:"],[1560,"For an application that already uses classes, pass the class to `builder.node` and provide\n`name: 'User'`. The default class check uses `instanceof` or the constructor on the prototype.\nUse this as an alternative to the ref above, with a loader that returns class instances."],[1369,"For an async source, the same field can use an async generator. Replace its resolver with:"],[2988,"For an ordinary, path-independent policy, `runScopesOnType: true` moves type checks to GraphQL\nobject completion, including selections containing only `__typename`. Denial then produces an error\nat the field returning the object. It still does not prevent the loader from running. Review its\nexecution compatibility and override limitations.\nKeep the parent-grant pattern below on the default field-level execution: parent grants are not\nresolved at the same response path when scopes run through `isTypeOf`."],[1580,"For APIs where you have the full array available you can use `resolveArrayConnection`, which works\njust like `resolveOffsetConnection` and accepts the same options."],[354,"For applied directive metadata, see Directives. GraphQL.js `printSchema`\ndoes not preserve applied custom directives; see Printing Schemas\nwhen choosing an output format for downstream tools."],[2910,"For cases where the required scopes depend on the value of the requested resource you can use a\nfunction in the `authScopes` option that returns the scope map for the field."],[1749,"For containers or a remote Agent, configure a reachable receiver address and set\n`OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_TRACES_ENDPOINT` to its `/v1/traces` endpoint. See\nDatadog's OTLP Agent setup\nfor the matching deployment configuration."],[2380,"For cursor-based pagination with page info and total counts, use `t.prismaConnection` instead. See\nConnections."],[2408,"For cursor-based pagination, use `t.relatedConnection`."],[1727,"For custom span hierarchies, the plugin exports `pathToString(info)`, `getParentSpan(context, info)`,\nand `createSpanWithParent(context, info, createSpan)`. The latter caches a span on the request\ncontext and passes the closest cached parent span to your callback. Use a fresh context for each\noperation so this cache belongs to that operation."],[1446,"For documentation on how to write plans, see the Grafast documentation."],[2699,"For example the query:"],[2193,"For example, a post's `commenters` connection pages through comments but returns each comment's\nauthor. The helper takes a model name or a Prisma type ref, plus `query`, `defaultSize`, `maxSize`,\n`totalCount` and `args`. `totalCount` takes `true`, but not a function."],[2387,"For example, if `collection` already orders posts by title and `query` orders by creation date,\ntitle stays the primary sort and creation date breaks ties. It's usually simplest to put ordering\nonly in `query.orderBy`."],[414,"For example, if `nickname`'s resolver throws `new Error('Nickname unavailable')`,\n`nullable: true` makes only `nickname` null. Without that override, the builder's non-null default\nmakes the whole response's `data` null."],[2897,"For example, if you want to re-throw errors thrown by authorization functions you could do this by\nwriting a custom `unauthorizedError` callback like this:"],[1376,"For example, this alternative field resolves its success branches explicitly using the\n`CreateResult` and `UpdateResult` types above:"],[1613,"For example, to add a field on the interface:"],[1682,"For fe