ish the user's identity."],[2357,"For this query:"],[484,"For types not described in the `SchemaTypes` type provided to the builder, including types that can\nnot be added there like Unions and Enums, you can use a `Ref` returned by the\nbuilder method that created them in the `type` parameter. For types created using a class\n(Objects or Interfaces) or Enums created using a typescript\nenum, you can also use the `class` or `enum` that was used to define them."],[635,"For types that reference each other, TypeScript may need ref creation and `implement` to be separate\nstatements, as in the walkthrough above. See circular references for details."],[2262,"For variants stored in the base model's table, `upsert()` can match a unique key belonging to a\ndifferent variant. For example, `Task.variant('bug').upsert(...)` can update a feature with that\nkey and return it as a bug. Check the existing task's kind before choosing whether to create or\nupdate when your mutation must preserve it."],[2382,"For writes, or anything else that runs the query itself, use `resolve` instead. It receives the\nselected Collection. See Mutations."],[2769,"Forgetting to spread the `query` argument from `t.prismaField` or `t.prismaConnection` into your\nprisma query can result in inefficient queries, or even missing data. To help catch these issues,\nthe plugin can warn you when you are not using the query argument correctly."],[2777,"From a checkout of the Pothos repository, with Node.js 22 or newer:"],[36,"Full Documentation"],[1881,"function or `[function, { message?, path? }]`, or an array of either"],[2964,"Gate the `node` and `nodes` fields so lookups require a scope before\nanything loads."],[2952,"Gate the lookup fields"],[2824,"Generalized auth functions with field specific arguments"],[515,"Generating a schema.graphql file with graphql-code-generator"],[508,"Generating client types"],[2759,"Generator options:"],[2632,"Generators"],[7,"Getting started"],[1966,"Getting started"],[823,